// export-latency.kql
// Description: Measures the latency between a span's recorded timestamp and its Log Analytics
// ingestion time (ingestion_time()), as a proxy for how long the App Insights -> Log Analytics hop
// of the pipeline takes before a row is even available to the Event Hub export rule (#35). Large or
// growing latency here is an early warning sign for downstream Event Hub/Function lag, independent
// of anything Arize-side.
// Expected output shape: a table with columns [bucket (1h), p50LatencySeconds, p95LatencySeconds,
// maxLatencySeconds], one row per hour bucket in the last 24 hours. Healthy result for this demo's
// low-volume synthetic traffic: p95 well under a few minutes; any multi-hour latency indicates an
// export pipeline stall worth investigating before blaming the Function/Arize hop.
AppDependencies
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
| extend ingestionLatencySeconds = datetime_diff('second', ingestion_time(), timestamp)
| summarize
    p50LatencySeconds = percentile(ingestionLatencySeconds, 50),
    p95LatencySeconds = percentile(ingestionLatencySeconds, 95),
    maxLatencySeconds = max(ingestionLatencySeconds)
    by bucket = bin(timestamp, 1h)
| order by bucket asc
